course: dictionary
lesson: 9310
title: Speculation: guessing, not knowing
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Speculation means guessing about something when you do not know all the facts. «There is speculation that the star will leave the team» means people are guessing. Nobody has confirmed it yet.
explain: Look for clues that a sentence is about a guess: words like might, maybe, rumour, or «nobody knows for sure». Speculation can also be about money. «Speculation is buying because you hope the price will go up» means buying something to sell later for more, which is risky.
explain: Ask yourself: is this confirmed? If not, speculation may be the right word. Then test your meaning: «There is guessing that the star will leave the team» still makes sense, so guessing is a good meaning.
fact: Speculation means guessing about something without knowing all the facts.
fact: A speculation is one such guess or idea.
fact: In money talk, speculation means buying shares, land or houses, hoping to sell them later for more money. It is risky.
fact: «Pure speculation» means a guess with no proof behind it.
fact: A bubble is when prices rise far above real value and then burst.
exercise: «There is speculation that the star will leave the team.» What does speculation mean here? | Official news from the team manager | A song the star has written | Proof that the star is leaving | *Guessing, because nothing is confirmed yet
exercise: In money talk, what is speculation? | Painting pictures of houses | Giving money to charity every year | *Buying shares, land or houses, hoping to sell later for more, which is risky | Counting coins in a jar
exercise: In science, what is a speculation? | A type of experiment with a fixed result | An idea that has been tested many times | A fact from a textbook | *An idea not yet tested
test: «Pure speculation» means what? | Loud gossip from a crowd | Proven facts | Careful measurements | *Guesses with no proof behind them
test: «Some see new money for the world, others mostly speculation; nobody knows for sure who is right.» What does mostly speculation suggest? | A new kind of money | *Risky buying and guessing, not solid proof | Something that has been proven | A long, careful study
exam: Which of these is a speculation, not a fact? | The sun rises in the east each morning | *Aliens will land on Earth next year, some people say | Two plus two makes four | Water boils at 100 degrees Celsius at sea level
